<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lex Ripuaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lex Ripuaria is the law code of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ripuarian-franks">Ripuarian Franks</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> region, written in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> in the 7th century, probably under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagobert-i">Dagobert I</a>. Based largely on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salic-law">Salic law</a>, it set out compensation payments for injuries and crimes, rules of procedure and property, and the status of different groups. It remained in use under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingians</a>.</p></div>
